From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:42:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Text: decode UTF-8, fontconfig fallback for missing
 glyphs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Text was rasterized byte by byte, so "「 TUESDAY 」" came out as Latin-1
garbage. Decode UTF-8 to code points and, when the wallpaper font has no
glyph (CJK brackets, symbols), take a face from fontconfig that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
